   "ref": "35–38",
   "en": "Very well — granted that, until now, no suitor has moved you, not in Libya, not before that in Tyre; that you turned down Iarbas, and the other chieftains that [Africa|17,18], rich in triumphs, breeds. But will you fight against a love that pleases you too?",
