  {
   "id": 3,
   "ref": "39–44",
   "en": "[Have you forgotten|1,2,3,4] whose lands you have settled in? On one side, the cities of the Gaetulians hem you in — a people unconquerable in war — with the unbridled Numidians, and the pitiless Syrtis; on the other, a land parched with drought, and the Barcaeans, raging far and wide. Why should I even mention the war brewing from Tyre, and the threats from your own brother?'",
   "en_marked": "[Have you forgotten|1,2,3,4] [whose|5] [lands|7] [you have settled in|6]? [On one side|8], the [cities|10] of the [Gaetulians|9] [hem you in|17] — a [people|11] [unconquerable|12] [in war|13] — [with|14] the [unbridled|16] [Numidians|15], [and|18] the [pitiless|19] [Syrtis|20]; [on the other|21], a [land|24] [parched|22] with [drought|23], [and|25] the [Barcaeans|27], [raging|26] [far and wide|25]. [Why|28] [should I|32] {even|Not in the Latin. Added to bring out the rhetorical force of quid dicam, a question that needs no answer.} [mention|32] the [war|29] [brewing|31] [from Tyre|30], [and|33] the [threats|34] from your {own|Not in the Latin. Added for emphasis: germani means her brother Pygmalion, which makes the threat more personal.} [brother|33]?'",
